  "question": {
    "text": "The number of chlorine atoms in bithionol is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Bithionol is an antibacterial, anthelmintic, and algaecide.&nbsp;Bithionol&nbsp;(the compound is also called bithional) is added to soaps to impart antiseptic properties. It is&nbsp;aryl sulfide that is diphenyl sulfide in which each phenyl group is substituted at position 2 by hydroxy and at positions 3 and 5 by chlorine.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4f66acd1-18fa-40b4-b31e-9536fe1272b3-image.png\" style=\"width: 254px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>So, as we can see in the structure it has total of 4 chlorine atoms.</p><p>Chlorine atoms&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
